{"questions":[{"question_id":"lsbmht85","content":"Given below are two statements :<br><br>\n<b>Statement (I)</b> : The <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> group in Aniline is ortho and para directing and a powerful activating group.\n<br><br>\n<b>Statement (II)</b> : Aniline does not undergo Friedel-Craft's reaction (alkylation and acylation).<br><br>\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the <b>most appropriate</b> answer from the options given below :\n","chapter":"compounds-containing-nitrogen","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","isBonus":false,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2024-online-1st-february-morning-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2024 (Online) 1st February Morning Shift","permalink":"given-below-are-two-statements-brbr-bstatement-i-jee-main-chemistry-rh8ngmcapypzexle","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"Given below are two statements :<br><br>\n<b>Statement (I)</b> : The <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> group in Aniline is ortho and para directing and a powerful activating group.\n<br><br>\n<b>Statement (II)</b> : Aniline does not undergo Friedel-Craft's reaction (alkylation and acylation).<br><br>\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the <b>most appropriate</b> answer from the options given below :\n","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are correct"},{"identifier":"B","content":" Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>The given statements pertain to aniline, a primary amine where the amino group (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is directly attached to a benzene ring. Let's analyze the statements:</p>\n\n<p><b>Statement (I):</b> The <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> group in Aniline is ortho and para directing and a powerful activating group.</p>\n\n<p>This statement is correct. The amino group (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) in aniline is an electron-donating group due to the lone pair of electrons on the nitrogen atom. It increases the electron density on the benzene ring, particularly at the ortho and para positions. This in turn makes the ortho and para positions more reactive toward electrophilic aromatic substitution reactions. Therefore, the amino group is considered to be an ortho and para director and is one of the most powerful activating groups in the context of electrophilic aromatic substitution reactions.</p>\n\n<p><b>Statement (II):</b> Aniline does not undergo Friedel-Craft's reaction (alkylation and acylation).</p>\n\n<p>This statement is also correct. Aniline does not undergo Friedel-Crafts alkylation or acylation reactions. The reason for this is twofold: Firstly, the Lewis acid catalysts used in Friedel-Crafts reactions (such as AlCl<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.099ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -320.2 436.6 485.8\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) react with the amino group to form a complex that deactivates the benzene ring toward further reaction. Secondly, the strong interaction between the Lewis acid and the lone pair on the nitrogen can lead to a salt formation rather than the desired alkylation or acylation of the benzene ring. Moreover, the acidic conditions can lead to protonation of the amino group, converting it into an <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.706ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.826ex\" height=\"2.57ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -823.8 2133.1 1136\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1533,411.6) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-296.6) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> group, which is meta-directing and deactivating, further inhibiting the reaction.</p>\n\n<p>Given this analysis, the correct option is:</p>\n\n<p><b>Option A:</b> Both Statement I and Statement II are correct.</p>"},"hi":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"नीचे दो कथन दिए गए हैं :<br><br>\n<b>कथन (I)</b> : एनिलाइन में <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> समूह ऑर्थो और पैरा निर्देशक और एक शक्तिशाली सक्रियक समूह है।\n<br><br>\n<b>कथन (II)</b> : एनिलाइन फ्रीडेल-क्राफ्ट्स प्रतिक्रिया (अल्काइलेशन और एसिलेशन) में प्रतिक्रिया नहीं करता।<br><br>\nउपरोक्त कथनों के आधार पर, नीचे दिए गए विकल्पों में से <b>सबसे उपयुक्त</b> उत्तर चुनें :\n","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"कथन I और कथन II दोनों सही हैं"},{"identifier":"B","content":" कथन I और कथन II दोनों गलत हैं"},{"identifier":"C","content":"कथन I सही है लेकिन कथन II गलत है"},{"identifier":"D","content":"कथन I गलत है लेकिन कथन II सही है"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>दिए गए कथन एनिलीन से संबंधित हैं, जो एक प्राथमिक एमीन है जिसमें एमिनो समूह (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) सीधे बेंजीन वलय से जुड़ा होता है। आइए कथनों का विश्लेषण करें:</p>\n\n<p><b>कथन (I):</b> एनिलीन में <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> समूह ऑर्थो और पैरा निर्देशक तथा एक शक्तिशाली सक्रियकारी समूह है।</p>\n\n<p>यह कथन सही है। एनिलीन में एमिनो समूह (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) नाइट्रोजन परमाणु पर एकाकी इलेक्ट्रॉन युग्म के कारण एक इलेक्ट्रॉन-दाता समूह है। यह बेंजीन वलय पर इलेक्ट्रॉन घनत्व को बढ़ाता है, विशेष रूप से ऑर्थो और पैरा स्थितियों पर। यह बदले में ऑर्थो और पैरा स्थितियों को इलेक्ट्रॉनस्नेही एरोमैटिक प्रतिस्थापन अभिक्रियाओं के प्रति अधिक क्रियाशील बनाता है। इसलिए, एमिनो समूह को ऑर्थो और पैरा निर्देशक माना जाता है और इलेक्ट्रॉनस्नेही एरोमैटिक प्रतिस्थापन अभिक्रियाओं के संदर्भ में सबसे शक्तिशाली सक्रियकारी समूहों में से एक है।</p>\n\n<p><b>कथन (II):</b> एनिलीन फ्रीडेल-क्राफ्ट्स अभिक्रिया (एल्किलीकरण और एसिलीकरण) नहीं देती है।</p>\n\n<p>यह कथन भी सही है। एनिलीन फ्रीडेल-क्राफ्ट्स एल्किलीकरण या एसिलीकरण अभिक्रियाएं नहीं देती है। इसका कारण दोहरा है: प्रथम, फ्रीडेल-क्राफ्ट्स अभिक्रियाओं में उपयोग किए जाने वाले लुईस अम्ल उत्प्रेरक (जैसे AlCl<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.099ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -320.2 436.6 485.8\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) एमिनो समूह के साथ अभिक्रिया करके एक संकुल बनाते हैं जो बेंजीन वलय को आगे की अभिक्रिया के प्रति निष्क्रिय कर देता है। द्वितीय, लुईस अम्ल और नाइट्रोजन पर एकाकी युग्म के बीच प्रबल अन्योन्यक्रिया बेंजीन वलय के वांछित एल्किलीकरण या एसिलीकरण के बजाय लवण निर्माण की ओर ले जा सकती है। इसके अलावा, अम्लीय परिस्थितियां एमिनो समूह के प्रोटॉनीकरण की ओर ले जा सकती हैं, जो इसे <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.706ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.826ex\" height=\"2.57ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -823.8 2133.1 1136\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1533,411.6) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-296.6) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> समूह में परिवर्तित करती हैं, जो मेटा-निर्देशक और निष्क्रियकारी है, जो अभिक्रिया को और अधिक बाधित करता है।</p>\n\n<p>इस विश्लेषण को देखते हुए, सही विकल्प है:</p>\n\n<p><b>विकल्प A:</b> कथन I और कथन II दोनों सही हैं।</p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"aromatic-amines","type":"mcq","year":2024,"tags":["multi_statements"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2024-online-1st-february-morning-shift","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are correct"},{"identifier":"B","content":" Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p>The given statements pertain to aniline, a primary amine where the amino group (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is directly attached to a benzene ring. Let's analyze the statements:</p>\n\n<p><b>Statement (I):</b> The <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> group in Aniline is ortho and para directing and a powerful activating group.</p>\n\n<p>This statement is correct. The amino group (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) in aniline is an electron-donating group due to the lone pair of electrons on the nitrogen atom. It increases the electron density on the benzene ring, particularly at the ortho and para positions. This in turn makes the ortho and para positions more reactive toward electrophilic aromatic substitution reactions. Therefore, the amino group is considered to be an ortho and para director and is one of the most powerful activating groups in the context of electrophilic aromatic substitution reactions.</p>\n\n<p><b>Statement (II):</b> Aniline does not undergo Friedel-Craft's reaction (alkylation and acylation).</p>\n\n<p>This statement is also correct. Aniline does not undergo Friedel-Crafts alkylation or acylation reactions. The reason for this is twofold: Firstly, the Lewis acid catalysts used in Friedel-Crafts reactions (such as AlCl<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.099ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -320.2 436.6 485.8\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) react with the amino group to form a complex that deactivates the benzene ring toward further reaction. Secondly, the strong interaction between the Lewis acid and the lone pair on the nitrogen can lead to a salt formation rather than the desired alkylation or acylation of the benzene ring. Moreover, the acidic conditions can lead to protonation of the amino group, converting it into an <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.706ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.826ex\" height=\"2.57ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -823.8 2133.1 1136\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1533,411.6) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-296.6) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> group, which is meta-directing and deactivating, further inhibiting the reaction.</p>\n\n<p>Given this analysis, the correct option is:</p>\n\n<p><b>Option A:</b> Both Statement I and Statement II are correct.</p>"}]}